      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T02:08:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming src tree symlinks are read through the symlink seems like a hack to make specifying dependencies easier. I think the behavior in this cl is more correct, where if you want to access both the symlink and the file it points at you have to list them both as dependencies yourself. Maybe we could address this when we eventually add full action sandboxing to ninja.",
